# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Plague City" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting the quest
0	section	Talking to Edmond
1	line	Player	Hello old man.
1	line	Edmond	Sorry, I can't stop to talk...
1	line	Player	Why, what's wrong?
1	line	Edmond	I've got to find my daughter. I pray that she is still alive...
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What's happened to her?
2	line	Player	What's happened to her?
2	line	Edmond	Elena's a missionary and a healer. Three weeks ago she managed to cross the wall into West Ardougne. No one's allowed to cross the wall in case they spread the plague.
2	line	Player	Plague?
2	line	Edmond	Not that long ago, West Ardougne was hit by a deadly plague. They had the wall built to try and keep it contained. No one is allowed to enter the city now apart from the mourners.
2	line	Edmond	They say the plague is a horrible way to go... That's why Elena felt she had to go help. She said she'd be gone for a few days but we've heard nothing since.
2	line	Player	Maybe I could help find her?
2	line	Edmond	Really, would you? I've been working on a plan to get into West Ardougne, but I'm too old and tired to carry it through. But you on the other hand, you should have no problem.
2	select	Start the Plague City quest?
2	option	Yes.
3	line	Player	Where should I start?
3	line	Edmond	If you're going into West Ardougne you'll need protection from the plague. My wife made a special gas mask for Elena with dwellberries rubbed into it.
3	line	Edmond	They help to repel the plague apparently. We need some more though...
3	line	Player	Where can I find these dwellberries?
3	line	Edmond	The only place I know of is McGrubor's Wood, just west of Seers' Village. The berries are bright blue so they're easy to spot.
3	line	Player	Okay, I'll go and get some.
3	line	Edmond	The foresters keep a close eye on it, but there is a back way in.
3	action	end
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	On second thoughts, I'd better not.
3	line	Edmond	Well if you hear anything about Elena please tell me.
3	line	Player	I will. Goodbye.
3	action	end
1	option	Well, good luck finding her.
2	line	Player	Well, good luck finding her.
2	action	end
